{"kind":"assert","text":"Request bbbd3a48, rendering a promise as the GitHub assignee, is blocked on the outbound charter request 33329544 awaiting Hugh. That dependency is not visible from either record, so the work reads as unstarted when it is actually waiting.\n\nWHY IT IS BLOCKED. The request itself names the obstacle: there is no mapping from a workroom actor to a GitHub account, and inventing one would be the dishonesty this connector exists to avoid. Assigning the token's owner as a stand-in would make the issue say Hugh is working on something Claude promised, which the log contradicts. The mapping has to be stated by someone with authority to state it, and the charter is where it belongs — it already names the connector, owner, repository and actor.\n\n33329544 asks Hugh to state and ratify a scoped outbound charter. Until that exists and carries a mapping, the assignee rendering cannot be implemented honestly. I confirmed the work is genuinely undone: nothing under internal/connector mentions an assignee.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED AND GOT WRONG ON THE WAY. Looking at what awaits Hugh, a script of mine reported that the README review head 6ef29521 no longer merges cleanly, and I was about to report that it would waste Hugh's time. The definitive check disagrees: git merge-tree against main exits zero and produces a clean tree 464cd7af, with no conflict output. The head merges. I could not reproduce the failing result and am recording the correction rather than the alarm. What is true of 0e66e7be is only that the request is stale, and that its head is Hugh's own work.\n\nSTATE OF THE THREE ITEMS AWAITING HUGH, as measured. 33329544, the outbound charter, is not stale and is the only one genuinely actionable; it blocks bbbd3a48. 0e66e7be, the README review at 6ef29521, is stale as a request but its head merges cleanly. 8159b5ae, asking for a decision on proposal 3d5ef955, is stale; it concerns world-staleness propagating through every basis edge including request, promise and report edges that describe no code — which is the phenomenon that has produced most of the stale rows I have worked around all session.\n\nWHY THIS IS RECORDED RATHER THAN LEFT AS A MESSAGE. A request sitting unstarted on my board with no visible reason invites someone to pick it up and invent the mapping, which is the one outcome its author was trying to prevent. Naming the dependency is what keeps that from happening after this session ends.\n\nNothing here is mine to unblock. I am not proposing a mapping, because proposing one is the same act as inventing one when the person with authority has an open request to state it.","body":{"blocked":"bbbd3a48","on":"33329544","reason":"no authoritative actor-to-GitHub-account mapping"}}